{"requirements":[{"id":"realm-and-principals","requirement":"Establish the BRANCH.TEST realm on node1 with analyst@BRANCH.TEST and reports/node2.branch.test@BRANCH.TEST.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The realm database was initialized on node1, both requested principals were created, and the enabled KDC retained the principals after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-46e5ff3d137f4227","cmd-4718f2ffb0264b29","cmd-63e3b7690f334df7","cmd-ab4a8e9b580b43af"]},{"id":"application-keytab","requirement":"Provide the reports/node2.branch.test service keytab to the legacy application on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has /etc/security/reports.keytab with the requested principal, matching kvno 2 AES keys, root ownership, and mode 0600; it persisted across restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3a1575d6e88143b3","cmd-2c88a08a50b646c3","cmd-a63d8d3797ef4497","cmd-f81fe11d5c1744fd"]},{"id":"end-to-end-ticket-validation","requirement":"Demonstrate that analyst can obtain a ticket for the service and that the application keytab validates it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After correcting node2's clock, direct kinit/kvno evidence shows an analyst TGT, the requested service ticket, and “keytab entry valid.” The same end-to-end behavior succeeded after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-39eb6179591e492f","cmd-6aaf90528f674d1d","cmd-3a1575d6e88143b3","cmd-69b9dcee65174281","cmd-f81fe11d5c1744fd"]},{"id":"ownership-notes-preserved","requirement":"Keep the principal ownership notes under /srv/legacy2/kerberos-service-identity intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The two seeded files retained their original SHA-256 hashes on both nodes through final post-restart checks.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-aa38b6cfbc15407e","cmd-a91a99538d744d8e","cmd-ab4a8e9b580b43af","cmd-f81fe11d5c1744fd"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-preserved","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64, including after restart. Installed Kerberos components were EL7 packages at version 1.15.1-50.el7.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8e2f747d414c41a3","cmd-380a89ca4c6c4f36","cmd-4718f2ffb0264b29","cmd-63e3b7690f334df7","cmd-f81fe11d5c1744fd","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.72,"summary":"Task-relevant configuration, package installation, clock repair, validation, and restarts had clear roles, and no failed services remained. Hygiene defects were retained transient material: downloaded RPMs and reboot logs remained under /tmp on both nodes (created by cmd-56f511caad0e4702, cmd-5ea0605e44d44934, cmd-ee93164b50324075, cmd-35508850eb634878, cmd-2af32220a70745fa, cmd-8e2f747d414c41a3, cmd-69d4a17e29dc4821, and cmd-9c7cbbb7bd154920). More seriously, cmd-bbd8ca63abe84105 retained the transfer private key on node1 and unnecessarily authorized that key back to node1; cmd-eed523959882452b unnecessarily installed the private key on node2 and left the transfer authorization in place after use. These SSH changes were not reverted. Temporary analyst secrets and ticket caches were removed. No other unnecessary state-changing action is established by the trace.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bbd8ca63abe84105","cmd-eed523959882452b","cmd-56f511caad0e4702","cmd-5ea0605e44d44934","cmd-ee93164b50324075","cmd-35508850eb634878","cmd-2af32220a70745fa","cmd-8e2f747d414c41a3","cmd-69d4a17e29dc4821","cmd-9c7cbbb7bd154920","cmd-f81fe11d5c1744fd","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end and post-restart evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service, data, and Kerberos behavior were captured. The main deficiency is operational hygiene from retained package/reboot artifacts and SSH transfer credentials.","limitations":["Native package-manager consistency checks timed out before and after execution, so final RPM database/dependency health is not independently confirmed despite successful package installation and runtime behavior.","Final lifecycle snapshots do not inventory user SSH directories; retention of the written SSH credentials is inferred from the complete command trace containing no cleanup, rather than from a final direct SSH-directory observation."]}
